{
  "about": "Every interface motion's times and easing (report.md step 8 and section 10.3). Rules from §21.8 (D3 (b)): every step lasts 150 to 250 ms and eases out, nothing overshoots its end value, a press squashes slightly, rewards fly into their counter, shake is never above 4 px. From §20.8: each motion names its reduced form, which drops swoops and particles but keeps one coin landing in its counter, and nothing repeats faster than three times a second. Times are in milliseconds from the motion's start; distances in points (the kit's UI.px turns them into pixels); sprites are pieces of client/ui/art/motion.json. check_curves.py holds this file to these rules.",
  "version": 1,
  "rules": {
    "shortest_ms": 150,
    "longest_ms": 250,
    "easings": [
      "cubic_out"
    ],
    "overshoot": false,
    "flash_hz_most": 3,
    "shake_px_most": 4,
    "shake_switchable": true
  },
  "easings": {
    "cubic_out": {
      "formula": "1 - (1 - t)^3",
      "godot": {
        "trans": "TRANS_CUBIC",
        "ease": "EASE_OUT"
      },
      "overshoot": false
    }
  },
