    "reward": {
      "about": "The result screen's reward sequence (rubric quality 5). The prize gathers and charges for the tier's anticipation_ms (0.3 to 1 s, longer for a rarer reward): gather starts it, the prize holds, and charge, marked ends_at burst, is placed to end at the burst (it starts its ms before); the payoff starts at the burst (its at_ms count from there): the burst, the reveal, and the coins flying in arcs to their counter, 60 ms apart. Each coin's landing runs on_landing: the counter rolls up by that coin's share and pulses. The pulse changes size, never brightness, so the landings are not flashes (§20.8); the burst is the one flash of a reward. The coins share one sprite strip (face, turn, edge, turn) at frame_ms a frame: a coin turning, at constant brightness. A rarer reward has more particles, a longer anticipation and a brighter, larger burst (tiers). Values named tier.<key> come from the reward's tier.",
